{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tag an effect with an identity so it can be cancelled later — by another effect, or imperatively from view code."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every effect the store runs is already cancelled on teardown: "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and the store’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":" cancel all in-flight effect tasks. That is enough for cleanup, but it is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"all-or-nothing","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — you cannot cancel one specific effect while others keep running."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyed cancellation adds that. You give an effect a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"cancel id","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and later cancel every effect running under that id with the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" effect or the imperative "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" method. Identity lives outside the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" type — it is still a plain closure — so nothing about reducer signatures changes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach for this when an effect outlives the action that started it: cancelling text-to-speech when the user skips, debouncing a search field, or tearing down a long-lived listener when a screen disappears."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Choosing-an-id","level":2,"text":"Choosing an id"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A cancel id is any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable & Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" value. Distinct ids are independent; effects sharing an id are cancelled together. A dedicated empty type reads well and can’t collide with another feature’s id:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["private enum SearchID: Hashable, Sendable {}","private enum SpeechID: Hashable, Sendable {}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Strings and enums work too — pick whatever is unambiguous in your domain."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Cancel-from-inside-a-reducer","level":2,"text":"Cancel from inside a reducer"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Return "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to tag the work, and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to stop it:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["case .startSpeaking(let text):","    return cancellable(id: SpeechID()) { send in","        for await word in speech.speak(text) {","            await send(.spokeWord(word))","        }","    }","","case .skip:","    \/\/ Stop any in-flight speech immediately.","    return cancel(id: SpeechID())"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the speaking effect is cancelled, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await"},{"type":"text","text":" loop ends at the next suspension point, exactly as it would on teardown."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Debounce-with-cancelInFlight","level":2,"text":"Debounce with `cancelInFlight`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Passing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cancelInFlight: true"},{"type":"text","text":" cancels any effect already running under the id "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" starting the new one — the whole of debounce in one line:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["case .queryChanged(let query):","    return cancellable(id: SearchID(), cancelInFlight: true) { send in","        try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(300))","        let results = try await api.search(query)","        await send(.results(results))","    }"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each keystroke re-dispatches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".queryChanged"},{"type":"text","text":"; the new effect cancels the previous sleeping one, so only the last query in a burst reaches the network."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Cancel-from-view-or-scene-code","level":2,"text":"Cancel from view or scene code"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When there is no reducer action to hang the cancellation on — a screen disappearing, a sheet dismissing — call "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" directly:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".onDisappear {","    store.cancel(id: SearchID())","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ids with nothing running are ignored, so it is always safe to call."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"What-it-does-not-replace","level":2,"text":"What it does not replace"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyed cancellation is not a substitute for resource cleanup. An effect holding a file handle, a network connection, or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"type":"text","text":" continuation should still release it — use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withTaskCancellationHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" or a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"defer"},{"type":"text","text":". Cancellation ends the task; it does not close what the task opened."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects that terminate on their own (a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await"},{"type":"text","text":" loop whose stream finishes) need no id at all. Only reach for a cancel id when something "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"else","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" has to stop the effect early."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtocanceleffects"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Cancel Effects"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"How-to Guides","anchor":"How-to-Guides","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"]}],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/AgentSkill":{"abstract":[{"text":"Install the bundled ","type":"text"},{"code":"swidux-ref","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" skill so your AI coding assistant has Swidux’s architecture rules and code templates on hand."}],"title":"Using the Swidux Agent Skill","role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/agentskill","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch":{"title":"Add a Version Killswitch","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaversionkillswitch","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","type":"topic","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Wire a remote-controlled blocker that prevents unsupported app versions from running, with an “Update” path back to the App Store.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with declarative event mapping and auto-identify.","type":"text"}],"title":"Add Analytics","role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAParentalGate":{"title":"Add a Parental Gate","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","type":"topic","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAPaywall":{"title":"Add a Paywall","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddapaywall","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","type":"topic","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app to gate features behind a subscription or lifetime purchase.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/cancelEffects()":{"title":"cancelEffects()","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/canceleffects()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancels all in-flight effects."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"cancelEffects","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddFeatureFlags":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values from a single JSON config."}],"title":"Add Feature Flags","role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddfeatureflags","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"title":"Building a Domain Plugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","type":"topic","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","title":"Swidux","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddICloudSync":{"title":"Add iCloud Sync","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddicloudsync","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","type":